y":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.3275094775012362,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.08740623658247341,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":4.2,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.02767460453454218,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":38.8,"_gate_margins":0.0023703015884470437,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":52.4,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.1486743584457932,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.014215019123875905,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":67.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.02994120635842346,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":50.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.85212,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Playtika Holding Corp., together with its subsidiaries, develops mobile games in the United States, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, the Asia Pacific, and internationally. The company owns a portfolio of casual and social casino-themed games. It distributes its games to the end customer through various web and mobile platforms and direct-to-consumer platforms. The company was founded in 2010 and is headquartered in Herzliya Pituach, Israel. Playtika Holding Corp. operates as a subsidiary of Playtika Holding UK II Limited.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert  Antokol | Co-Founder, Chairperson, CEO & President | Age 57 | Compensation: $5.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $868K ranks in the above the sector median among Communication Services peers. Each employee generates $167K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $26K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Playtika Holding Corp. is a small-cap communication services business with a $1.0B market cap on $2.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are contracting by -3.3pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 27% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 20-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $531M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 37.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 14.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 85% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -3.3pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 167% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Communication Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 84% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 57% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Communication Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Contrasting IMAX (NYSE:IMAX) & Playtika (NASDAQ:PLTK)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/contrasting-imax-nyseimax-playtika-nasdaqpltk.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794585534.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.935,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Playtika (PLTK) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/what-playtika-pltk-said-on-its-q3-earnings-call.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794172510.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]